// CotSC: English translation extracted from bg1300_citizens.d
// Original English strings preserved exactly. Translate text inside ~...~ only.

@1 = ~Respect our laws, citizen and abide by them.~
@2 = ~As someone who hails from Amn I got to say their laws are outlandish and straight up barbaric. They do not tolerate magic, unless you pay them. My niece was practising magic, completely harmless spells, and they she was visited by Cowled Wizards. Ridiculous. I am not at all surprised if the rumours about the alleged upcoming war turns out to be true.~
@3 = ~Have you got nothing better to do than speak to me?~
@4 = ~I am so ashamed that my kin caused all that havoc at Nashkel mines. It's shameful to our kind.~
@5 = ~I had a pleasure of meeting Entar Silvershield. He is a really good fella. I heard his daughter is a real handful.~
@6 = ~I wish this city wouldn't be crawling with dwarves. These smelly pests... poisoning the streets with odour of their impertinence.~
@7 = ~Stay cautious on the streets at night. Some shady figures roam around. Before you know it, your gold will be gone from your pockets.~
@8 = ~I am overjoyed that this city is so tolerating toward tieflings. I moved here all the way from Waterdeep and the level of hatred I encountered toward me was outraging. I did not choose my fiendish heritage, have I?~
@9 = ~I keep peace in the port area. If you do not adhere to the rules, Flaming Fist will be informed and you shall be put to trial.~
@10 = ~Don't bother me. I am just a common citizen. I know nothing. Whatever you want to ask me, I don't know the answer. Goodbye.~
@11 = ~I hope you aren't trying to plunder my kitchen. I have had enough problems with troublesome patrons recently.~
